      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: NIT: This traversal stops if `pair.ptr` is a `Target::GROUP`, even though rustc might natively link the transitive rlibs through the group (because GN flattens groups into `--extern` for intermediate crates). This means rlibs behind groups might be passed to the linker twice (once by rustc natively, once explicitly via `-Clink-arg` below). \n\nSince linkers gracefully handle duplicate static archives (`.rlib`), this is harmless in practice, but just something to be aware of.",
